{"id": "20549514", "revid": "48736052", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20549514", "title": "OGLE2-TR-L9b", "text": "OGLE2-TR-L9b is an extrasolar planet discovered by three undergraduate students from Leiden University, Netherlands.\nThe planet is about 4.5 times as massive as Jupiter and is the first discovered planet orbiting a fast-rotating hot star.\nInitially discovered while testing a method for investigating light fluctuations in the OGLE database, the planet's existence was later confirmed by follow-up observations from the ESO's Very Large Telescope in Chile."}
